02:13:11.985 --> 02:13:13.724
from the IPCC about

02:13:13.724 --> 02:13:16.641
whoa, it is here, it's irrevocable.

02:13:18.922 --> 02:13:21.005
I mean, it's no question.

02:13:22.695 --> 02:13:23.945
And you go, ah,

02:13:24.955 --> 02:13:26.785
I mean, at the same time,

02:13:26.785 --> 02:13:27.618
it's important that we have the opposite,

02:13:27.618 --> 02:13:29.285
which is like, yeah.

02:13:30.225 --> 02:13:33.002
And got it. Thank you for sharing.

02:13:33.002 --> 02:13:35.957
Thanks for such fantastic science.

02:13:35.957 --> 02:13:37.374
Let's go to work.

02:13:38.213 --> 02:13:39.046
And this is the work

02:13:39.046 --> 02:13:42.157
that can be done everywhere, by everyone.

02:13:42.157 --> 02:13:45.574
And we can absolutely meet the challenge.

02:13:47.454 --> 02:13:49.903
No question we need both.

02:13:49.903 --> 02:13:52.653
And so it's not that the science,

02:13:53.682 --> 02:13:55.343
or it's understandable

02:13:55.343 --> 02:13:57.836
that the science has been couched and threat and fear

02:13:57.836 --> 02:13:58.683
and all that sort of stuff.

02:13:58.683 --> 02:14:01.156
I mean the scientists didn't know how to communicate

02:14:01.156 --> 02:14:04.971
an activist took the science and used blame and shame

02:14:04.971 --> 02:14:06.564
and finger pointing as a way

02:14:06.564 --> 02:14:09.373
to thought they thought maybe that would make a difference.

02:14:09.373 --> 02:14:12.206
I don't know, but both were right.

02:14:13.196 --> 02:14:14.357
It's not that,

02:14:14.357 --> 02:14:18.214
but they didn't conform to neuroscience.

02:14:18.214 --> 02:14:20.475
Right, it's a natural,

02:14:20.475 --> 02:14:25.076
psychological reaction to not being heard, right?

02:14:25.076 --> 02:14:27.764
It's just frustration that builds into anger

02:14:27.764 --> 02:14:29.972
and it's well-intentioned,

02:14:29.972 --> 02:14:33.345
but it doesn't actually change minds or hearts.

02:14:33.345 --> 02:14:34.178
No.

02:14:35.084 --> 02:14:36.305
I think we're seeing that shift

02:14:36.305 --> 02:14:38.638
across all forms of activism

02:14:39.823 --> 02:14:43.283
because i mean you spoke about the gay rights movement.

02:14:43.283 --> 02:14:45.135
I mean, you see that in the vegan movement,

02:14:45.135 --> 02:14:47.602
like, all these sort of tried and true methods

02:14:47.602 --> 02:14:49.004
that have been used for years

02:14:49.004 --> 02:14:52.240
that just make people angry and divide people.

02:14:52.240 --> 02:14:53.274
We're now realizing,

02:14:53.274 --> 02:14:54.995
Hey, that's not such a good approach.

02:14:54.995 --> 02:14:56.054
Exactly, in fact,

02:14:56.054 --> 02:14:58.466
another figure ground shift from my point of view

02:14:58.466 --> 02:15:00.704
was vegan the plant rich.

02:15:00.704 --> 02:15:03.537
Vegan polarized, I mean, eat eggs.

02:15:04.923 --> 02:15:07.256
I mean, but plant rich, like

02:15:10.063 --> 02:15:11.864
I don't know if I coined it

02:15:11.864 --> 02:15:13.373
or I know the first time I used it,

02:15:13.373 --> 02:15:15.933
I hadn't seen it anywhere, but that was in Drawdown,

02:15:15.933 --> 02:15:17.254
which is rich.

02:15:17.254 --> 02:15:18.087
Like, first of all,

02:15:18.087 --> 02:15:20.035
that's a great word and plants...

02:15:20.035 --> 02:15:20.876
It's like gardening.

02:15:20.876 --> 02:15:23.053
Plants is a great word. People love plants,

02:15:23.053 --> 02:15:25.163
And so plant rich diet,

02:15:25.163 --> 02:15:27.874
is like, so that's an invitation

02:15:27.874 --> 02:15:29.755
come on in the water's fine.

02:15:29.755 --> 02:15:33.005
Find your way into the world of plants.

02:15:34.425 --> 02:15:37.116
You decide, you figure it out.

02:15:37.116 --> 02:15:39.374
But again, it was like a figure ground shift

02:15:39.374 --> 02:15:42.604
away from something that could cause people to resist

02:15:42.604 --> 02:15:45.786
to something that was invitational.

02:15:45.786 --> 02:15:47.466
And that's what regeneration is

02:15:47.466 --> 02:15:48.975
an invitation to participate

02:15:48.975 --> 02:15:51.555
is not, that's what it is come on in.

02:15:51.555 --> 02:15:53.283
It really is fine. It works.

02:15:53.283 --> 02:15:54.950
And why are you here

02:15:57.160 --> 02:15:59.924
at this point, at this time,

02:15:59.924 --> 02:16:01.122
given what we know,

02:16:01.122 --> 02:16:02.923
what's your purpose?

02:16:02.923 --> 02:16:04.854
What gives meaning to your life?

02:16:04.854 --> 02:16:07.314
That's the question everybody's asked.

02:16:07.314 --> 02:16:09.594
Yeah. we gotta end this in a couple of minutes,

02:16:09.594 --> 02:16:10.903
but I can't let you go

02:16:10.903 --> 02:16:14.404
without pulling on this last thread,

02:16:14.404 --> 02:16:18.883
which is, and it's related to the psychology piece

02:16:18.883 --> 02:16:21.962
that we were just discussing.

02:16:21.962 --> 02:16:22.795
How do you,

02:16:22.795 --> 02:16:24.481
let's say somebody is listening to this.

02:16:24.481 --> 02:16:25.944
They're super enthusiastic.

02:16:25.944 --> 02:16:27.024
They're good to go.

02:16:27.024 --> 02:16:27.904
They wanna translate

02:16:27.904 --> 02:16:31.071
that sort of emotionality into action.

02:16:33.384 --> 02:16:34.521
Like we talked about,

02:16:34.521 --> 02:16:38.762
but they're surrounded by a community of people

02:16:38.762 --> 02:16:41.734
or family members or colleagues, et cetera,

02:16:41.734 --> 02:16:43.635
that are unreceptive to this.

02:16:43.635 --> 02:16:46.113
And they wanna be able to communicate effectively

02:16:46.113 --> 02:16:47.704
their passion for this

02:16:47.704 --> 02:16:51.060
to be a change agent for others.

02:16:51.060 --> 02:16:53.303
So, given what we just talked about,

02:16:53.303 --> 02:16:54.763
what are some strategies

02:16:54.763 --> 02:16:59.024
for helping people communicate more effectively?

02:16:59.024 --> 02:17:01.073
Don't use the word climate,

02:17:01.073 --> 02:17:03.122
don't use the word global warming.

02:17:03.122 --> 02:17:05.613
Those are macro issues and are conceptual.

02:17:05.613 --> 02:17:07.842
And mean almost nothing to everybody really.

02:17:07.842 --> 02:17:09.952
I mean, we use the term,

02:17:09.952 --> 02:17:11.940
but they have no meaning.

02:17:11.940 --> 02:17:14.634
And most of the jargon and acronyms around climate

02:17:14.634 --> 02:17:15.554
have no meaning.

02:17:15.554 --> 02:17:17.214
They're completely conceptual.

02:17:17.214 --> 02:17:19.353
If you say somebody, 1 5C,

02:17:19.353 --> 02:17:20.543
what does that mean to anybody?

02:17:20.543 --> 02:17:21.376
Nothing.

02:17:21.376 --> 02:17:23.042
I mean, somebody can understand it,

02:17:23.042 --> 02:17:24.943
even do it to 2.7 F,

02:17:24.943 --> 02:17:27.155
I'm making, figure it out

02:17:27.155 --> 02:17:29.125
still means nothing.

02:17:29.125 --> 02:17:32.556
And so to move completely away from climate speak,

02:17:32.556 --> 02:17:35.606
because it's meaningless to most people

02:17:35.606 --> 02:17:37.965
and to speak in ways that are meaningful

02:17:37.965 --> 02:17:39.786
to the people who surround you.

02:17:39.786 --> 02:17:44.786
And to the thing about carbon sequestration, for example

02:17:44.906 --> 02:17:47.135
let's go back to soil, farming,

02:17:47.135 --> 02:17:52.135
which is the purpose of regen Ag is not to sequester carbon.

02:17:52.627 --> 02:17:54.127
That's an outcome.

02:17:55.076 --> 02:17:57.395
It's really important to understand the difference.

02:17:57.395 --> 02:17:59.897
The purpose of regen farm

02:17:59.897 --> 02:18:04.397
farming for a farmer is to actually change their life,

02:18:06.196 --> 02:18:07.687
to get out of debt,

02:18:07.687 --> 02:18:09.925
to stop using poisons,

02:18:09.925 --> 02:18:13.168
to poison their family or themselves, and so forth,

02:18:13.168 --> 02:18:15.225
to increase their profitability,

02:18:15.225 --> 02:18:17.904
to be proud of what they're doing

02:18:17.904 --> 02:18:21.296
to absolutely become more resilient to drought

02:18:21.296 --> 02:18:22.656
in too much water

02:18:22.656 --> 02:18:27.477
so that the soil can be a reservoir instead of dirt.

02:18:27.477 --> 02:18:29.345
I mean, you to create,

02:18:29.345 --> 02:18:31.767
to increase the pollinators for your crops,

02:18:31.767 --> 02:18:33.737
which are now dead and gone.

02:18:33.737 --> 02:18:35.994
I mean, it goes on and on and on,

02:18:35.994 --> 02:18:39.955
by the way, the outcome is more life in the soil

02:18:39.955 --> 02:18:44.178
and that life is measured by C carbon, okay.

02:18:44.178 --> 02:18:46.954
But that's an outcome, if somebody's paying for it.

02:18:46.954 --> 02:18:49.327
Hallelujah. It's another crop you've got going for you,

02:18:49.327 --> 02:18:51.144
but that is not the purpose.

02:18:51.144 --> 02:18:54.104
And so the same thing with climate,

02:18:54.104 --> 02:18:58.066
our purpose is to really take care of each other,

02:18:58.066 --> 02:19:01.384
to improve the wellbeing of humanity on this planet

02:19:01.384 --> 02:19:05.087
and all living creatures, all of life.

02:19:05.087 --> 02:19:06.915
And we do that.

02:19:06.915 --> 02:19:09.104
We reverse global warming,

02:19:09.104 --> 02:19:11.744
but if you start with reversing global warming,

02:19:11.744 --> 02:19:15.475
you've lost most people, right there.

02:19:15.475 --> 02:19:17.208
Because you're putting the outcome

02:19:17.208 --> 02:19:18.625
before the value.

02:19:20.558 --> 02:19:22.385
The value, purpose.

02:19:22.385 --> 02:19:23.844
But the thing that connects

02:19:23.844 --> 02:19:25.625
that doesn't connect

02:19:25.625 --> 02:19:28.875
I mean go to a party and somebody said,

02:19:31.454 --> 02:19:32.287
oh, what do you do?

02:19:32.287 --> 02:19:33.526
I'm a climate activist.

02:19:33.526 --> 02:19:35.103
And they're going, oh, good.

02:19:35.103 --> 02:19:35.936
Or just immediately.

02:19:35.936 --> 02:19:38.225
Everybody has some association

02:19:38.225 --> 02:19:39.856
with that negative or positive, right?

02:19:39.856 --> 02:19:41.204
Baggage comes into play.

02:19:41.204 --> 02:19:43.987
And everybody's made up their mind

02:19:43.987 --> 02:19:44.997
how they feel about it

02:19:44.997 --> 02:19:46.936
before the conversation even begins.

02:19:46.936 --> 02:19:48.726
I mean, I like what you said earlier,

02:19:48.726 --> 02:19:50.816
when you were talking about that town hall

02:19:50.816 --> 02:19:52.634
and just having people raise their hands

02:19:52.634 --> 02:19:55.408
and identify what their values are.

02:19:55.408 --> 02:19:56.241
Absolutely.

02:19:56.241 --> 02:19:59.408
Through that you discover this commonality,

02:19:59.408 --> 02:20:03.745
this like, shared sensibility that we can unite over.

02:20:03.745 --> 02:20:05.088
If you're sitting next to somebody

02:20:05.088 --> 02:20:06.624
and you say I'm a climate activist,

02:20:06.624 --> 02:20:07.763
I'm trying to save, the rainforests

02:20:07.763 --> 02:20:09.074
they are going, oh, cool.

02:20:09.074 --> 02:20:10.407
If you say like,

02:20:12.446 --> 02:20:13.665
oh, I'm trying to save the world

02:20:13.665 --> 02:20:15.297
which even more ineffective.

02:20:15.297 --> 02:20:16.714
But if you say...

02:20:17.703 --> 02:20:18.536
you sound like an asshole.

02:20:18.536 --> 02:20:20.556
Like( chuckles)

02:20:20.556 --> 02:20:22.977
Well, there's so much hubris in that.

02:20:22.977 --> 02:20:23.810
What are you doing?

02:20:23.810 --> 02:20:24.643
I'm saving the world.

02:20:24.643 --> 02:20:25.984
That's all for us,

02:20:25.984 --> 02:20:26.817
but you can't do anyway.

02:20:26.817 --> 02:20:27.650
But if you say

02:20:27.650 --> 02:20:28.483
I discovered this way,

02:20:28.483 --> 02:20:30.935
if smartphones are being thrown away.

02:20:30.935 --> 02:20:34.383
And what I started to do in this place in Peru,

02:20:34.383 --> 02:20:36.726
I started to nail them up to trees

02:20:36.726 --> 02:20:37.895
and connect them together

02:20:37.895 --> 02:20:41.074
with little tiny solar cells kept them charged.

02:20:41.074 --> 02:20:43.184
And that way the indigenous people there

02:20:43.184 --> 02:20:45.833
